============================================================
     Log Collection Utility - Command Line Interface        
============================================================


USAGE
-----
  ./logmgr [OPTIONS]

OPTIONS
-------
  --logPath, -l <path>    Specify the path for collected logs (required)
  --help, -h              Display this help message

  --error-codes, -e       Show all available exit codes and meanings


EXAMPLES
--------
  # Collect logs to specified directory
  $ logmgr -l ~/logs/issue_logs/

  # Launch GUI mode (no arguments)
  $ logmgr

IMPORTANT NOTES
---------------
  - Exclusive Modes: --logPath, --help, and --error-codes are mutually exclusive
  - No Arguments: GUI interface is launched
  - Path Required: --logPath/-l must be followed by a valid path
  - Path Format: Can be absolute, relative, or use ~ for home
  - Directory Creation: Non-existent paths will be created during collection
  - Existing Paths: Must have write permissions
